# SABOTAGE: T78 (spec §I5 helpdesk knowledge base + composer suggestion + deflection) —
# `Samen.Web.Support.KbReads.suggest_for_portal/4`'s re-verification refetch swaps
# `Post.:read_public` (org_id + status:published + visibility:public, the SAME gate
# `public_articles/2` and the portal browse use) for a raw `org_id`-only filter with
# `authorize?: false`. The vector index (`Samen.AI.Embeddings`) is candidate RETRIEVAL
# ONLY by design — every consumer is supposed to re-verify a hit's source record
# against its OWN scoped read before ever rendering it (defense in depth: a stale or
# over-broad vector must never surface content the reader is not otherwise authorized
# to see). This patch removes exactly that re-verification for the deflection path: an
# INTERNAL article that was ever embedded (e.g. published, then flipped internal, or an
# internal article some future caller embeds) now surfaces in the UNAUTHENTICATED
# portal's deflection suggestions the moment it semantically matches a visitor's typed
# subject/description — a real content leak that never touches `Post.:read_public`'s
# own filter at all (patches 102/103 are a DIFFERENT guarantee: this one is the
# candidate-retrieval-is-not-authorization discipline).
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/support/kb_reads_test.exs test/samen/web/portal_kb_live_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: DEFENSE IN DEPTH — an article embedded while public, then flipped to internal, never surfaces on the portal
# MUST_FAIL: an INTERNAL article (never public) never surfaces on the portal even if it ranks well
# MUST_FAIL: an internal article never surfaces in deflection even if it would rank well
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/support/kb_reads.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/support/kb_reads.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/support/kb_reads.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/support/kb_reads.ex
@@ -204,9 +204,8 @@ defmodule Samen.Web.Support.KbReads do
       query,
       fn hit_ids ->
         Mount.resource(kb_mount, Post)
-        |> Ash.Query.for_read(:read_public, %{org_id: org_id})
-        |> Ash.Query.filter(id in ^hit_ids)
-        |> Ash.read!(actor: nil, authorize?: true)
+        |> Ash.Query.filter(org_id == ^org_id and id in ^hit_ids)
+        |> Ash.read!(authorize?: false)
       end,
       opts
     )
